# CODEOWNERS — the agent-enablement contract for fams-v5-demo-environment (decision #17).
#
# The whole point of the tenant model is that AGENTS customize tenants freely and
# CI (`demo check` + the capture Action) is the safety net — not a human gate on
# every content change. So the customization surface has NO owner (an unowned
# path requires no review), while the SEAMS that change tool/CI/app behavior are
# human-gated to the platform team.
#
# GitHub semantics: the LAST matching pattern wins. We first leave everything
# unowned, then claim only the seams. Replace @fams/platform-team with the real
# team/handles once the org + team exist (placeholder for now).

# Free for agents (no required review — CI is the gate):
#   core/       — canonical modules (core-first changes; inheritance shows in the diff)
#   tenants/    — typed deltas, seeds, tenant-native modules
#   resolved/   — GENERATED + committed (regenerated by resolve/capture, never hand-owned)
# (left intentionally unowned)

# Human-gated seams — changing these changes how the platform itself behaves:
/tools/            @fams/platform-team
/.github/          @fams/platform-team
/app/src/demo/     @fams/platform-team
/CLAUDE.md         @fams/platform-team
